            stem: "A supply contract between two merchants for the sale of component parts said payment was due within 30 days of invoice. For two years, the seller accepted the buyer's payments on about the 45th day without objection and never told the buyer it would insist on strict compliance. When the buyer paid on day 45 again, the seller declared a default and cancelled the contract. The buyer sued for breach.",
